  and you need the booster in particular  though because with omicron there's some  invasion of the immune response not all  the immune response but some of it but  the booster helps restore the protection  that you get from your two doses so that  is the most important measure are we  keeping people out of the hospital are  we saving lives with that said you know  wherever possible we want to reduce the  number of infections because we want to  prevent people from getting long covered  we know there are still many people who  are unvaccinated including kids under  five we want to protect them also from  exposure to the virus  but now we're hearing dr murthy about uh  breakthrough  breakthrough cases with boosters we used  to be told that if you get your booster  it provides you maximum protection i  hear you say if you get it you're gonna  be okay but that's still not comforting  you get the booster because you think  i'm going to be protected now how are we  supposed to process this information and  not be afraid  as we look at the long lines of people  well it's  yeah it's a really important question  gail and i just want to say i recognize  that with omicron and all of this news  this can be a scary time for people and  it can be fatiguing as well right we've  been at this for two years but here's  how to think about the the booster shot  the booster reduces your chances of  certainly getting severely ill and it  reduces your chances of getting sick in  the first place but no vaccine is  perfect and especially against a foe  like omicron we know that there are  going to be some people who despite  getting boosted they may get what are  called breakthrough infections but those  infections are much more likely to be  mild uh compared to maybe somebody who  is not boosted or not vaccinated who may  have a you know a greater chance of  ending up in the hospital so the bottom  line is you have to isolate if you get a  break very well  if you get a breakthrough do you have to  isolate  yes so if you get an infection uh  whether you've infected been vaccinated  or not you should isolate because you're  at risk of spreading it to others  all right doctor as it relates to covert  it's oftentimes described as a fight so  sticking with the theme if i'm watching  a boxing match i can tell who's winning  so i have to ask you who's winning this  fight is it covet or or is it us  well we are certainly in a much better  place than we were a year ago and the  reason is this we have more tools in our  toolbox we have the vaccines and the  boosters we know our masks work to  reduce spread our testing can also be a  strategy to make gatherings safer  especially important before you get  together for the holidays and we know  how important ventilation is now not  something we fully appreciated a year  ago and so when you gather gathering in  well-vented ventilated places can also  make your gathering safer so we are in a  better place with better tools and  better knowledge and that's why i  actually feel confident despite omicron  coming on the scene that we have the  tools to get through this pandemic we've  got to stick together though in this  process we can't let this pandemic  splinter us  dr moorthy we're running out of time but  since you mentioned tools and you  mentioned testing there's a conversation  we've been hearing about in the medical  world about whether all the tests out  there including the antigen test at home  can actually detect omicron are you  aware of that conversation and can you  say this morning that all tests can  indeed detect omicron  we're absolutely aware of these  conversations and in fact making sure  that our tests are working working well  has been an important priority of the  fda since omicron came on the scene the  good news is that the data that they've  seen so far in their testing has been  reassuring that the vast majority of  tests that americans are using are  working and working well they're going  to continue to monitor this and make  sure that they  yeah are there are there certain tests  that americans should be aware of as  they go into the holiday gathering  period that you should stay away from  because they don't work  well the fda has listed publicly on its  website a few tests which it has some  concerns about but those don't include  the vast majority of tests that people  are buying over the counter in their  pharmacies so the bottom line is if  you're getting an over-the-counter test  you know this is an important tool that  you can use to help you make your  gathering safer and at this point we can  feel confident that those tests are  still serving us and serving as well  dr vivek morty thank you so much for  joining us and answering the questions  that we all need to know we appreciate  you

